      "operation": "Silver City",
      "task": "Mine/Booby trap",
      "gridRef": "YT076433",
      "friendlyForce": 100,
      "enemyForce": 0,
      "friendlyKilled": 0,
      "friendlyWounded": 4,
      "enemyKilled": 0,
      "enemyWounded": 0,
      "units": [
        "3 Field Troop, 1 Field Squadron",
        "B Company, 1 Battalion, Royal Australian Regiment"
      ],
      "subUnits": [],
      "report": "B Company reported that three soldiers (including one US soldier) had been wounded when a claymore mine was detonated in front of a Mule (a light transport vehicle) extracting rice from a captured cache. The 2 Australians wounded were 38151 Sapper M. Livingstone and 42853 Sapper D.J. Peters, both of 3 Field Troop.",
      "archivalSource": "AWM95, item 7/1/61, 1 Battalion, Royal Australian Regiment, Narrative, Annexes, 1-31 Mar 66, p. 22."
    },
    {
      "id": 66,
      "url": "/battlemap?incident=66",
