      "report": "Coy detonates M16 mine\n\nYS671607, ELMS 1 FD SQN AND A/6RAR/NZ DET M16 MINE. RESULTS:1 AUST KIA, 4 AUST WIA. ) YS671607, ELMS 1 FD SQN AND A/6RAR/NZ DET M16 MINE. RESULTS: 1 AUST KIA, 4 AUST WIA. (M) A. 500M NE OF INCIDENT IS OLD HARBOUR POSN (PROB EX 8RAR) OF PL SIZE. ABOUT 1 KM NE OF THAT POINT IS OLD COY HARBOUR POSN (POSS ALSO 8RAR). B. 5M SW OF INCIDENT IS CLEARING (HELI PAD ETC). MINE WAS LAID ON BULLOCK TRACK LEADING TO CLEARING. C. AT LEAST 4 MEN HAD PASSED OVER THE MINE PRIOR TO ITS DETONATION. 8RAR HAD BEEN THRU THIS AREA PRIOR TO A/6RAR/NZ\u0027S MOV INTO THE AREA. WOULD APPEAR MINE WAS LAID FOL 8RAR\u0027S MOV OUT OF AREA. OC A/6RAR/NZ BELIEVES THAT ALL OTHER TRACKS LEADING INTO THAT CLEARING FROM OTHER DIRECTIONS WOULD ALSO BE MINED. THERE WAS VC MINE MARKER POINTING TWDS THIS MINE. IT WAS BRANCH BROKEN AND LEFT POINTING TWDS MINE. ADDITIONAL INFO. A. MINE WAS PLACED IN SAND PATCH ABOUT 5M IN DIA. THE BULLOCK CART TRACKS PASSED THRU CLEARING. B. MINE MARKER WAS ON BUSH SIDE OF MINE AND ON BULLOCK CART TRACK. C. EN OBVIOUSLY APPRECIATED THAT CLEARING WOULD BE USED BY OUR TPS AS LZ FOR INSERTION/EXTRACTION OR MAINTDEM AND HAS PROB PLACED MINES ON ALL ACCESS TRACKS INTO CLEARING. D. SHOULD ALSO BE EXPECTED THAT OTHER OBVIOUS CLEARINGS USED AS LZ\u0027S, PARTICULARLY ONES WITH MARKED EXIT TRACKS, COULD BE MINED.  \n\nJungle 7 Km s of Xuyen Moc",
      "archivalSource": "AWM109 Ops 1ATF [C]; Intsum, AWM95 1/4/186.pdf p93"
    },
